QuestGuidance.Register("en",232,{
[7393]="70027B1D\n1\tTalk to Acca in the gardens of Isengard\tYou are Gríma Wormtongue, advisor and servant to Saruman the White. He has been visited by Radagast the Brown, and you and Acca are waiting to hear if your master has any commands for you.\n2\tTalk to Acca in the gardens of Isengard\tYou have overheard Saruman speaking of some troubling things, but Acca can make no sense of them.\n3\tTalk to Saruman in the gardens of Isengard\tSaruman is in the gardens of Isengard and wants to speak with you.\n4\tListen to Acca continue his tale\tAcca's story continues.\n5\tTalk to Acca near the gates of Isengard\tAcca is waiting to speak with you.\n6\tSee to Gandalf's horse while Acca escorts the Wizard to Saruman\tYou are to take care of Gandalf's horse while Acca brings the Wizard to speak with Saruman.\n7\tListen to Acca's story continue\tListen to Acca's story continue.\n8\tTalk to Acca outside Orthanc\tAcca is near the steps of Orthanc, listening to the conversation of Gandalf and Saruman. You should speak with him.\n9\tTalk to Saruman on the steps of Orthanc\tSaruman is on the steps of Orthanc.\n10\tListen to Acca's story continue\tListen to Acca continue his story.\n11\tTalk to Acca on the pinnacle of Orthanc\tAcca has come to the pinnacle of Orthanc with a basket of bread for Gandalf. You should talk to him.\n12\tTalk to Acca on the pinnacle of Orthanc\tAcca wants to speak with you on the pinnacle of Orthanc.\n13\tListen to Acca's story continue\tAcca's story continues.\n14\tFind Saruman within Orthanc and tell him of Acca's sympathies\tYou must find Saruman within Orthanc and tell him of Acca's sympathies.\n",
[7394]="7006E4B9\n1\tInvestigate the commotion at the gate with Inkanûsh\tA commotion at the nearby gate has drawn your attention.\n2\tObserve the confrontation at the gate and be ready to intervene if it comes to violence\tThe guardsmen at the gate have stopped a group of warriors from entering the city.\n3\tTalk to the Umbari guardsman\tAn Umbari guardsman has asked you to speak on behalf of Inkanûsh.\n4\tStand ready to prevent the outbreak of violence\tYou have helped to ease some of the tension between the two groups at the gate, but you should remain on guard just in case.\n5\tTalk to Hármelak at the gate\tHármelak has come to the gate, and she has questions for you.\n6\tEnter the Citadel of the Winds as a guest of the Kindred\tYou and Inkanûsh have been invited to attend the meeting of the Kindred of the Coins with Shâra Mizâdi within the Citadel of Winds.\n7\tTalk to Rahâzi in the Citadel of Winds\tRahâzi has stayed behind to speak with you in the Citadel of Winds.\n8\tAttend the meeting of the Kindred of the Coins and Shâra Mizâdi of Renewed Hamât\tThe Kindred of the Coins meets with Shâra Mizâdi of Renewed Hamât to discuss the relationship between their two powers and the days to come.\n9\tTalk to Shâra Mizâdi in the Citadel of Winds\tShâra Mizâdi desires to speak with you before the attendees disperse.\n10\tTalk to Hármelak in the Citadel of Winds\tHármelak has indicated that she wants to speak with you before you leave.\n",
[7395]="70017945\n1\tTalk to Huldar\tHuldar is standing in the centre of Othrikar. The dwarf Huldar is waiting to speak to you.\n2\tSupport the Othrikar sentries against the Dourhands\tThe Dourhands plan to attack Othrikar, and you have been charged with keeping the dwarf-defenders fighting as long as possible.\n3\tSupport the Othrikar sentries at Huldar's position\tHuldar has been wounded in battle, and now the Othrikar sentries up by the mines are without their Rune-keeper. You must fill in for Huldar before it is too late.\n4\tTalk to Huldar\tHuldar is up by the mines of Othrikar. You have repelled the attack on Othrikar and should speak now to Huldar.\n",
[7396]="70018F16\n1\tTalk to Haldir\tYou have been summoned to an audience with Lord Celeborn of Lórien, and should speak now to Haldir.\n2\tListen to what Celeborn has to say to you\tCeleborn has called you to an audience in Caras Galadhon.\n3\tTalk to Haldir\tHaldir is waiting to speak with you about the worries of Lord Celeborn.\n",
[7397]="7001482A\n1\tRecover artifacts from Balin's expedition (total: 6)\tA grim silence pervades the mine, interrupted only by the alien sounds of the Gredbyg. Discover what you can of Balin's mining expedition.\n2\tYou have found the picks of Balin's miners, and naught else but danger.\t\n",
[7398]="70009E0F\n1\tSpeak to Eliot Bencroft\tRangers have taken up position at three camps on the island of Rantost. Defend the Rangers from attacks by tomb-robbers and their allies.\n",
[7399]="7004D3CE\n1\tExamine the corpse of Thorog\tExamine the corpse of Thorog.\n2\tExamine the rust spot\tExamine the rust spot.\n3\tExperience the vision\tExperience the vision.\n",
[7400]="7003FDBD\n1\tLearn if Tenval shares your uneasy disquiet\tTenval has felt a curious disturbance and wishes to speak with you.\n2\tLearn if Dûgden knows what has caused this disturbance\tDûgden is beneath the Mountain, in the Paths of the Dead. He shares your curse, and your feeling that something has changed.\n3\tWatch the living interlopers pass, and learn their intentions\tA number of living Men have entered the paths beneath the Mountain, intruding upon your demesnes.\n4\tListen to the arguments of Tenval and Drugât\tOne of the living Men is the Heir of Isildur, and he has called your kind to the Stone of Erech. This has caused a split among your people: Tenval and Drugât argue the merits of following the Heir or ignoring his summons.\n5\tTalk to Tenval and learn his intention\030Talk to Dûgden and learn his intention\tTenval and Dûgden were your closest friends when you walked the earth as a living man, in the days before the Curse. Now they must decide where their course lies, as must you.\n6\tMake your choice: follow either Aragorn or Drugât\tTenval and Dûgden were your closest friends when you walked the earth as a living man, in the days before the Curse. They have decided where their paths lead, and now you must do the same.\n7\tWitness the actions of your potential allies\tYou have made your decision, and must now deal with the consequences.\n",
[7401]="700337F6\n1\tWalk out onto the Bridge of Khazad-dûm\tThe bridge of Khazad-dûm lies in the east of Nud-melek. You should walk out onto the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.\n2\tObserve what came to pass upon the bridge\tA scene unfolds before you on the Bridge of Khazad-dûm. You should observe the scene of what came to pass upon the bridge.\n3\tReturn to the goat to travel back\tThe goat you brought here is back a ways, east of the bridge. You should return to the goat to head back to the First Hall.\n",
[7402]="7005A1C6\n1\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed\tUnder the cover of darkness you have come with Derwent Bindweed to the meeting place in southern Bree-town.\n2\tStand by Derwent Bindweed and look fearsome\tUnder the cover of darkness you have come with Derwent Bindweed to the meeting place in southern Bree-town.\n3\tDefeat Bill Ferny's rough fellows\tUnder the cover of darkness you have come with Derwent Bindweed to the meeting place in southern Bree-town.\n4\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed\tYou have helped Derwent Bindweed stand up to Bill Ferny's demands.\n",
[7403]="700443DB\n1\tTalk to Haley on the road through Enedwaith\tHaley is on the road north through Enedwaith, and she has some words for you before you continue.\n2\tTalk to Bingo on the road through Enedwaith\tBingo is on the road through Enedwaith, preparing to deal with the Orc blockade. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Bloody Graham, the brigand leader\tThe brigand leader has motioned for you to speak to him.\n4\tKill all the brigands\tThe brigands will not let you pass, and must be slain.\n5\tLet Bingo have his say, but remain alert\tBingo has something to say to the brigands.\n6\tTalk to William at the blockade\tOne of the former brigands has motioned for you to speak with him.\n7\tExamine the treasure coffer William wants to give Bingo\tWilliam told you that some of the plunder was left behind by the Orcs, and he wants Bingo to have it.\n8\tTalk to Bingo at the blockade\tBingo is at the blockade in northern Enedwaith.\n",
[7404]="70034C1A\n1\tTalk to Oter\tThe rebuilding of Thrymm's Farm is underway. Oter has brought tools to the fields, and would like your help preparing the fields to produce crops for Forlaw.\n2\tFollow Oter to the western fields\tThe rebuilding of Thrymm's Farm is underway. Oter has brought tools to the fields, and would like your help preparing the fields to produce crops for Forlaw.\n3\tDefeat Warg-riders from the west (total: 4)\tThe farmers were prepared to begin working the fields, but the enemy has begun a surprise attack on Thrymm's Farm!\n4\tFollow Oter to the centre of Thrymm's Farm\tThe farmers are gathering near the barn, and are concerned that Ragnold may not be safe. He was on the far side of the farm when the western side was attacked.\n5\tDefeat Warg-riders from the south (total: 4)\tThe enemy is attacking from the south and are trying to trap you and the farmers on Thrymm's Farm while they burn it down.\n6\tTalk to Oter\tOter and the others have been cornered near the barn. The enemy is burning the farm to the ground. The chances of the farmers escaping and making a run for Forlaw are slim.\n7\tDefend Thrymm's Farm from the final assault\tLaudh has sent the captain of this band of Warg-riders to attack you and the farmers. He seems intent on capturing the farmers for some nefarious purpose.\n8\tObserve what Laudh has to say\tLaudh is capturing the farmers and leaving you at Thrymm's Farm, to either die there or to inform Forlaw of what happened. He is convinced Núrzum will kill you eventually.\n",
[7405]="70009323\n1\tSearch for Thrór's hammer\tSearch Skorgrím's tomb for Thrór's hammer.\n2\tDefeat Faerdamil\tDefeat Faerdami, a fell spirit who has taken possession of Thrór's hammer.\n",
[7406]="70037DB3\n1\tTalk to Horn and approach the king\tHorn is inside Meduseld, waiting to approach the king.\n2\tWitness the confrontation of Gandalf and Théoden, and allow harm to come to none\tInside Meduseld, Gandalf appeals to Théoden. Will the king heed the warning he brings?\n3\tTalk to Gandalf in Meduseld\tInside Meduseld, Gandalf has revealed his nature and his good intentions to Théoden King. What will the king make of the tidings he brings?\n4\tWitness the confrontation of Gandalf and Théoden, and allow harm to come to none\tInside Meduseld, Gandalf appeals to Théoden. Will the king heed the warning he brings?\n5\tTalk to Gandalf in Meduseld\tGandalf is in Meduseld and has attempted to lift the veil from Théoden's eyes as it concerns the plight of his people.\n",
[7407]="7005AF6C\n1\tTalk to Kyrstig\tThe plan to rescue Ausma begins with Kyrstig.\n2\tFind Ausma\tYou need to find Ausma.\n3\tStand by with the Scout Trio\t\n4\tBreak ice block (total: 3)\tAusma is frozen in a block of ice!\n5\tEscape with Ausma\tYou have to escape!\n",
[7408]="70003284\n1\tSpeak to Langlas\tLanglas requires your assistance to find and free Avorthal. You should watch each other's backs, lest you fail.\n2\tSpeak to Langlas\tYou have made progress into the Dourhand camp, but the effort was not easy, and Langlas has advised you rest before continuing on. You should let Langlas know when you are ready to go on.\n3\tSpeak to Langlas\tThis is the heart of the camp. Skorgrím's lieutenant is waiting for you. Talk to Langlas when you are ready to confront the villain and learn what happened to Avorthal.\n4\tSpeak to Langlas\tHakon Ironfist has been defeated, but it appears that Avorthal is not here. Speak to Langlas when you are ready to return to the hunting lodge.\n",
[7409]="7000066D\n1\tTalk to Reniolind\tReniolind is somewhere within the Marshwater Fort, west of the Mustering Cave. With his dying breath, the Ranger Mundol begged you to save Reniolind, another of his kindred, from Amdir's murderous rampage.\n2\tDefeat Amdir\tDefeat Amdir. Amdir was hiding in the deepest depths of the ruins and struck down Reniolind, then turned his attention to you.\n3\tDefeat Morin\tAmdir called forth a giant spider-queen before fleeing. Kill the spider and speak with the dying Ranger.\n4\tTalk to Reniolind\tReniolind lies dying on the floor of the caves. Reniolind has shown you a secret path under the Midgewater Marshes in the caves beneath the ruins. At the end, you found Amdir waiting. Amdir mortally wounded Reniolind, then fled. The dying Ranger wishes to speak with you.\n",
[7410]="7006C6E3\n1\tSpeak with Raphûz to begin the assault\t This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSpeak with Ashâmi to return to Urmâkh\tYour assault was successful, but the madness of the cultists weighs on Ashâmi and Raphûz. You should make haste and return to Urmâkh.\n",
[7411]="7004426C\n1\tRide across the Pelennor toward Minas Tirith\tYou can hear the sound of fighting ahead of you, in the middle of the Pelennor. Someone needs your help!\n2\tTalk to Faramir on the Pelennor Fields\tFaramir, Captain of Gondor, is beset on all sides by the forces of the enemy! You must help him reach Minas Tirith!\n3\tStand beside Faramir, and defend him from his foes\tFaramir has fallen from his horse! He seems to have suffered a terrible injury.\n4\tTalk to Gandalf on the Pelennor\tGandalf has crossed the field in the company of Prince Imrahil and his swan-knights, and he motions for you to speak with him.\n5\tRide for the gates of Minas Tirith\tGandalf has commanded you to ride for the city of Minas Tirith, while he follows with Prince Imrahil and the wounded Faramir.\n",
[7412]="7003A2AE\n1\tApproach Thane Mágla in the Mead Hall\tThane Mágla is sitting at his table. Mágla has asked you to speak with him.\n2\tShare mead with Mágla\tThe mead can be found on the table. Mágla has asked you to share a drink with him.\n3\tListen to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You should listen to Thane Mágla.\n4\tTell Mágla no\tMágla can be found at the table. Mágla sees no hope for Rohan. You should disagree with him.\n5\tTell Mágla a story of your adventures in the Eastemnet\tMágla can be found at the table. Mágla sees no hope for Rohan. You should tell him of your journeys in the Eastemnet.\n6\tChallenge Mágla to lead once more\tMágla can be found at the table. Mágla is beginning to believe that hope remains. You should challenge him.\n7\tListen to Mágla\tMágla is at the table in the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You should wait with Mágla as he decides what action to take.\n8\tTravel out of the Mead Hall with Mágla\tMágla can be found in the Mead Hall. You should travel outside to confront the White Hand with Mágla.\n9\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tMágla is in Middlemead. You should fight through Middlemead with Mágla.\n10\tFight through Middlemead with Thane Mágla\tMágla is in Middlemead. You should aid Mágla in escaping Middlemead.\n11\tDefeat Hildulf\tHildulf can be found at the traders' pavillion in Middlemead. You have encountered Hildulf and Uruks, and should now defeat them.\n12\tFlee Middlemead with Thane Mágla\tHorses can be found to the south-east of the traders' pavillion. You should now escape Middlemead.\n13\tTalk to Thane Mágla\tThane Mágla can be found outside the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You have escaped the White Hand forces and made your way to the horses. You should speak to Thane Mágla and flee!\n",
[7413]="70046C49\n1\tWalk with the Rangers of Ithilien\tThe Rangers of Ithilien were patrolling to the north-east of Henneth Annûn. Anborn is telling you a tale of strange travellers in Ithilien. You should listen closely.\n2\tListen closely to Anborn's tale\tThe Rangers of Ithilien spied the barren camp-site and moved to investigate. Anborn is telling you a tale of strange travellers in Ithilien. You should listen closely.\n3\tListen closely to Anborn's tale\tThe Rangers of Ithilien then spoke to the strange Halflings. Anborn is telling you a tale of strange travellers in Ithilien. You should listen closely.\n",
[7414]="700443C3\n1\tTalk to Bingo in Draigoch's lair\tBingo is inside the entrance to Draigoch's Lair, hoping to rescue Theodore Gorse before it is too late!\n2\tTalk to Haley in Draigoch's lair\tHaley has followed you to a ledge overlooking the sleeping dragon.\n3\tClimb down the rope to reach the floor of Draigoch's lair\tTheodore is on the floor of Draigoch's lair, and you need to climb down to reach him.\n4\tTalk to Bingo on the floor of Draigoch's lair\tBingo is on the floor of Draigoch's lair, and he wants to talk to you about something urgent.\n5\tSneak by the sleeping dragon with Bingo\tYou have found Theodore in Draigoch's lair!\n6\tTalk to Theodore in Draigoch's lair\tYou have found Theodore in the depths of Draigoch's lair.\n7\tLeave the lair with Theodore, Haley, and Bingo\tThe dragon stirs awake!\n8\tRun to the rope and escape from Draigoch's lair\tThe dragon is awake! You must make it to the rope before the lair fills with fire! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n9\tTalk to Theodore outside Draigoch's Lair\tYou have escaped from the dragon's lair... but just in time!\n",
[7415]="7004549D\n1\tGo down into the cellar\tGo down into the cellar in Bâr Nadhron and find Akhiz.\n2\tShow Akhiz the ransom\tShow Jarl Akhiz that you have brought the ransom.\n3\tTalk to Lacheg\030Talk to Togbor\tGo past the opened gate and see that the hostages are all right.\n4\tReturn to Akhiz\tNow that you have seen Lacheg and Togbor, return to Jarl Akhiz to complete the ransom.\n5\tPlace the ransom in the chest\030Create a distraction\tNow that you have seen Lacheg and Togbor, return to Jarl Akhiz for the ransom payment and choose which of the brothers to heed.\n6\tLeave the cellar!\tIt is time to leave the cellar in Bâr Nadhron.\n",
[7416]="70054565\n1\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. You have woken from a short rest to find the other Stout-axes in your cell awake as well.\n2\tFinish your rations\tYour rations can be found on a chunk of rubble near your bunk in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. Awoken by tremors and unlikely to find more rest, Lethi has suggested that you finish your rations before cultists of the Order of the Eye return to the dungeons.\n3\tCollect your plate\tYour emptied plate of rations can be found near your bunk in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. You should add it to the pile of plates near the gate to your cell.\n4\tTalk to Vaski\tVaski can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. After setting your plate down, Vaski has called you over. You should talk to Vaski.\n5\tTell Vaski no and ask him to share what he heard\tVaski can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. Vaski has heard several disquieting rumours in the Dark Tower and wishes to share them with you.\n6\tListen to Vaski and Lethi\tLethi and Vaski can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. Eager to share rumours while the Order of the Eye is absent, Vaski desires to tell you of what he has heard.\n7\tTalk to Lethi\tLethi can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. Frustrated with Vaski's recklessness, Lethi has put an end to the conversation.\n8\tLie down in your bunk and try to rest\tYour bunk can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. After a tense exchange between Lethi and Vaski, Lethi has suggested that you all try to rest in your bunks before dawn.\n9\tTry to rest\tYou are trying to rest.\n10\tTalk to Núluzagar\tNúluzagar can be found in the dungeons of Barad-dûr. You brief rest was interrupted by the harsh voice of the cultist, Núluzagar. You should hearken to Núluzagar before his patience wears thin.\n",
[7417]="700272AB\n1\tTalk to Andreg\tYou should speak with Andreg to learn his plan.\n2\tFollow Andreg to the Slade of Shadows.\t\n3\tTalk to Andreg\tSpeak with Andreg at the Slade of Shadows.\n4\tPlace the Token of the Goat on the first altar\030Place the Token of the Ox on the second altar\030Place the Token of the Stag on the third altar\tThe three altars can be found between the trees at the heart of the Slade of Shadows. Andreg instructed you to place the tokens of the gurach on the altars within the Slade of Shadows.\n5\tTalk to Andreg\tAndreg is hiding near the Slade of Shadows. You should return to Andreg at once.\n6\tWait with Andreg to see what happens\tWait with Andreg to see what happens.\n7\tStop the elhudan and defeat the Tribunal of Shadows\tDefeat the Tribunal of Shadows.\n8\tTalk to Andreg\tAndreg is lying among the shards of the Dutegelh. You should see if there is anything you can do to help Andreg.\n9\tCollect the Token of the Goat from the first altar\030Collect the Token of the Ox from the second altar\030Collect the Token of the Stag from the third altar\tThe tokens of the gurach are upon the altars at the heart of the Slade of Shadows. Andreg instructed you to collect the tokens of the gurach and return to him.\n10\tTalk to Andreg\tAndreg is lying mortally wounded among the shards of the Dutegelh at the heart of the Slade of Shadows. You should bring the tokens of the gurach to Andreg at once.\n",
[7418]="7002BFA3\n1\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Search the camp for survivors\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. No living person seems to be left in Grimbold's camp.\n2\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Search the camp for survivors\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. No living person seems to be left in Grimbold's camp.\n3\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith before he goes\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. You have encountered Candaith, and even though you know you are asleep, it is still painful to see him.\n4\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith before he goes\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. You have encountered Candaith, and even though you know you are asleep, it is still painful to see him.\n5\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith at the gate before he goes\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. Candaith is waiting for you by the entrance to Grimbold's camp.\n6\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Morflak and resist your fear\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. Morflak looms large in your memory, casting his shadow over all things.\n7\tYou are held in the grip of a dream\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\n8\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith on the shore of Lake Evendim\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. Candaith is waiting for you on the shore of Lake Evendim.\n9\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Golodir on the shore of Lake Evendim\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. Golodir stands before you on the shore of Lake Evendim.\n10\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Walk with Candaith and see what he shows you\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. Lothrandir stands before you on the shore of Lake Evendim.\n11\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Calenglad on the shore of Lake Evendim\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams. Calenglad stands before you on the shore of Lake Evendim.\n12\tYou are held in the grip of a dream.\tYour mind is disturbed by troubling dreams.\n13\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Talk to Candaith.\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Candaith stands before you once more, looking puzzled about something.\n14\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Samwise Gamgee on the banks of the Anduin\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.\n15\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Frodo Baggins on the banks of the Anduin\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.\n16\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Merry Brandybuck on the banks of the Anduin\030Listen to Peregrin Took on the banks of the Anduin\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.\n17\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Aragorn on the banks of the Anduin\030Listen to Legolas on the banks of the Anduin\030Listen to Gimli on the banks of the Anduin\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.\n18\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Listen to Boromir on the banks of Anduin\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.\n19\tYou are held in the grip of a dream.\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.\n20\tYou are held in the grip of a dream.\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Familiar faces have emerged from the fog of sleep.\n21\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. Examine the enormous sword that rises from the swamp before you\tYou are held in the grip of a dream. A giant sword rises from the misty swamp before you.\n22\tYou are held in the grip of a dream.\t\n",
[7419]="7002EE6A\n1\tTalk to Getfleda\tTalk to Getfleda.\n2\tHear Brunstan's side of the story\030Hear Sperling's side of the story\tTalk to Brunstan and Sperling.\n3\tTalk to Getfleda\tTalk to Getfleda and let her know what her friends had to say.\n4\tTalk to the children observing the fight between Brunstan and Sperling\tTalk to the children observing the fight between Brunstan and Sperling and learn if any of them saw what happened.\n5\tTalk to Getfleda\tTalk to Getfleda.\n",
[7420]="70027A0A\n1\tTalk to Tecwin\tTecwin kneels before you. Speak with him to discuss his plans.\n2\tTalk to Elder Déin\tSpeak with Elder Déin as he addresses the warriors.\n3\tChoose 4 soldiers to assist you\tElder Déin has asked you to choose four of his finest soldiers to join you in your attempt to destroy the siege engines of the Dunlending army.\n4\tTalk to Gwin\tSpeak with Gwin at the front lines. The Boar-clan will move out and attack the main camp, while you destroy as much of the camp as possible.\n5\tDestroy the first siege-engine\tDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.\n6\tDestroy the next siege-engine further in the camp\tDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.\n7\tDestroy the next set of siege-engines\tDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.\n8\tDestroy the final siege-engines\tDestroy any siege-engines that you come across in the camp.\n9\tTalk to Elder Déin quickly\tSpeak with Elder Déin in the centre of the conflagration.\n10\tDefeat Dunlending siege-captain\tDefeat the Dunlending siege-captain quickly.\n11\tTalk to Elder Déin\tSpeak with Elder Déin again.\n12\tFlee on Elder Déin's horse\tFlee upon Elder Déin's horse before the chance to survive is no more!\n",
[7421]="7002FA0E\n1\tTalk to Pippin by the camp-fire\tPippin is at the camp-fire on Parth Galen. You're worried, and should talk to your friends. Pippin is young and might need a friendly word.\n2\tTalk to Merry by the camp-fire\tMerry is sitting by the camp-fire at Parth Galen. You should talk to Merry to see if he is as concerned as you are.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn by the camp-fire\tAragorn is standing by the camp-fire on Parth Galen.\n4\tTalk to Boromir by the camp-fire\tBoromir has returned to the camp-fire on Parth Galen.\n5\tFrodo may be in danger! Stay with Aragorn!\tFrodo may be in danger! You have to stay with Aragorn!\n6\tUse your hobbit-sense to learn where Frodo has gone\tYou need to use your plain old hobbit-sense to figure out what has happened to Frodo!\n7\tGet back to the boats, Sam!\tFrodo needs to get back to the boats if he plans to leave for Mordor alone, and that means you need to get back to the boats if you are to catch him!\n8\tSwim out into Nen Hithoel and find Frodo's boat!\tFrodo has already taken one of the boats! You have to swim as best you can out into the lake to reach him before he gets too far away!\n9\tTalk to Frodo on the boat\tFrodo must be on this boat!\n",
[7422]="7002EEF8\n1\tTalk to Béortnoth\tBéortnoth wishes to speak with you.\n2\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the first leg of the attack\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the first leg of the attack.\n3\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the second leg of the assault\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the second leg of the assault.\n4\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the third leg of the assault\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the third leg of the assault.\n5\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the fourth leg of the assault\tFight alongside Béortnoth and Wadel on the fourth leg of the assault.\n6\tTalk to Béortnoth\tSpeak with Béortnoth.\n",
[7423]="700413C4\n1\tSpeak to Arvaethor\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tYou and Arvaethor enter the cave. You should speak to Arvaethor.\n2\tDefeat Orcs under the mountain (total: 5)\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tPush the Orkish forces further into the mountain.\n3\tPush the Orkish forces further into the mountain\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tPush the Orkish forces further into the mountain.\n4\tDefeat the Orc chieftain\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tDefeat the Orc chieftain.\n5\tStay in the cave and learn of what is happening\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tDead seep into the room. You should stay in the cave and learn of what is happening.\n6\tEscape the Dead and return to where you entered the cave\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tEscape the Dead and return to where you entered the cave. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n7\tSpeak with Arvaethor\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tSpeak with Arvaethor at the head of the cave.\n",
[7424]="70058C82\n1\tTalk to Agnar Brokentooth\tAgnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz. Agnar Brokentooth has led you to Ushkútoz to aid in sabotaging the Orcs' trench-tunnel and the defeat of Kraznákh, a lieutenant of Gorgar the Ruthless.\n2\tFight through Ushkútoz and find Kraznákh\tAgnar Brokentooth is leading the attack on Ushkútoz. You should follow Agnar Brokentooth and defeat the Orcs inhabiting Ushkútoz as you search for Kraznákh.\n3\tClear the central chamber of Ushkútoz\tThe central chamber can be found deep within Ushkútoz. You have found no sign of Kraznákh, but the central chamber of Ushkútoz is filled with Orcs. You should defeat them before continuing your search for Kraznákh.\n4\tTalk to Agnar Brokentooth\tAgnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz. You have defeated the Orcs in the central chamber of Ushkútoz, but you have found no sign of Kraznákh. You should talk to Agnar.\n5\tRemain alert!\tAgnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz. Agnar fears Kraznákh has lured you into an ambush. You should remain alert.\n6\tConfront Kraznákh\tKraznákh can be found in Ushkútoz. You have been trapped in the central chamber of Ushkútoz by Lieutenant Kraznákh and his Orcs. You should confront Kraznákh.\n7\tDefeat Kraznákh's Orcs and survive the ambush\tKraznákh's Orcs can be found in Ushkútoz. After trapping you in the central chamber of Ushkútoz, Kraznákh has set his Orcs upon you. You must defeat them.\n8\tDefeat Lieutenant Kraznákh\tKraznákh can be found in Ushkútoz. After you and Agnar defeated his retinue, Kraznákh has entered the fray in a fury. You must defeat Lieutenant Kraznákh.\n9\tTalk to Agnar Brokentooth\tAgnar Brokentooth can be found in Ushkútoz. With the sudden aid of Lági Helmbiter and Reithvald Red-ember, you and Agnar Brokentooth have defeated Lieutenant Kraznákh. You should talk to Agnar Brokentooth.\n",
})
